Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 03:28:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: VMware Ops + Cloud Ops copilot expansion, start module
 split

- Fix dead /api/l1-copilot/vmware route (UI called it, route never
  existed on main -- button has been 404ing in prod).
- Add SP.vmware and SP.cloudops dedicated system prompts (deeper than
  generic l1support: vCenter/vRA/vRO/VCD/NSX/PowerCLI/Terraform +
  Azure/AWS/AVS/VMC/GCVE aware).
- Add /api/l1-copilot/vmware-script (PowerCLI/Terraform/vRO/REST
  script generation) and /api/l1-copilot/cloud-ops routes.
- L1 shell: add Script Generator subpanel + "Open Full VMware
  Operations Module" launch link to the VMware SME section; add new
  Cloud Ops nav section/panel (Azure/AWS paste-and-diagnose).
- New standalone html/l1-copilot/vmware-copilot.html module page:
  Dashboard (health strip, static pending live vCenter wiring), SME
  Guidance, Script Generator, vRA Admin Assistant (endpoint creation
  wizard + AI validation), Cloud Director workflow overview, Upgrade
  Assistant. Reads ticket context relayed from the L1 shell on load.
  First slice of the doc's "role-based Copilot modules sharing one
  AI engine + ticket context" architecture.
- relay.core.js/relay.schema.json: register VMWARE_COPILOT and
  CLOUD_COPILOT domains; also fixed L1COPILOT, which the L1 shell was
  already writing to via TSM.relay.write() but was never registered
  (silent failure, caught by try/catch) -- and added missing TSM_NOC
  prefix to the schema allowlist while in there.

Verified locally: server boots clean, all three new routes return
500 (Groq host not in sandbox network allowlist) instead of 404,
400 validation still fires on missing input, both L1 shell and new
VMware module page load 200, relay.core.js confirmed serving the new
domain keys. Not yet verified end-to-end against a live Groq key.
